I wouldn't have called it difficult - I never really felt like I was in 
danger of failing, and it didn't delay acquiring the main instadeath 
antidotes like poison resistance, reflection and MR.

It was fairly trivial really, albeit slightly harder than I was expecting 
as I was a little short on equipment when I reached the castle and delayed 
filling the final parts of my AK till after Gehennom. But I'm not sure how 
much of this was due to the fact of shopless, and how much was the RNG 
being mean - for example, I only got 1.8 more wishes than the absolute 
minimum (and I had to compromise and plan for one of those), and I didn't 
find a single bag or a /WoC, when I usually do find several of each outside 
shops. I didn't have to resort to dipping every fountain above DL20 in the 
hope of wishes though...

As a single conduct, polypileless is probably more trivial as it's pretty 
simple to fill out an AK with the castle wand, even if it does mean 
"wasting" a wish on a =oFA or a can of grease. While shopless probably 
denies you around the same number of useful items, you have the added 
inconvenience of being unable to ID the ?oID.

I think the triviality of genoless depends upon your stage of ability in 
the game - I actually prefer to save my ?oGeno to curse and fill out 
my AK anyway, so genoless is pretty much the default for me (I would have 
declined throne genocides in this game too though), which I suppose means 
it's harder than genoless for me. On the other hand, someone who has 
problems with a specific monster type would probably find shopless easier 
I think.

This ascension was certainly an awful lot easier than my wishless genoless 
polypileless survivor, but then I wouldn't describe that as trivial!


